#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:56
msgid "Install development tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:58
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install -y \\\n"
"  cmake \\\n"
"  gcc-c++ \\\n"
"  git \\\n"
"  make \\\n"
"  patch \\\n"
"  python3-colcon-common-extensions \\\n"
"  python3-mypy \\\n"
"  python3-pip \\\n"
"  python3-pytest \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-cov \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-mock \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-repeat \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-rerunfailures \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-runner \\\n"
"  python3-rosdep \\\n"
"  python3-setuptools \\\n"
"  python3-vcstool \\\n"
"  wget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:81
msgid "Build ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:84
msgid "Get ROS 2 code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:86
msgid "Create a workspace and clone all repos:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:88
msgid ""
"$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_rolling/src\n"
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling\n"
"$ vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/rolling/"
"ros2.repos src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:95
msgid "Install dependencies using rosdep"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Dnf-Update-Admonition.rst:5
msgid ""
"ROS 2 packages are built on frequently updated RHEL systems. It is always "
"recommended that you ensure your system is up to date before installing new "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Dnf-Update-Admonition.rst:8
msgid "$ sudo dnf update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:99
msgid ""
"$ sudo rosdep init\n"
"$ rosdep update\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -y --skip-keys \"fastcdr rti-"
"connext-dds-7.7.0 urdfdom_headers\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:106
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:108
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at build or runtime. See the :doc:`guide <../RMW-"
"Implementations/Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work "
"with multiple RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:112
msgid "Build the code in the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:114
msgid ""
"If you have already installed ROS 2 another way (either via RPMs or the "
"binary distribution), make sure that you run the below commands in a fresh "
"environment that does not have those other installations sourced. Also "
"ensure that you do not have ``source /opt/ros/${ROS_DISTRO}/setup.bash`` in "
"your ``.bashrc``. You can make sure that ROS 2 is not sourced with the "
"command ``printenv | grep -i ROS``. The output should be empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:119
msgid ""
"More info on working with a ROS workspace can be found in :doc:`this "
"tutorial <../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-"
"Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:121
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_rolling/\n"
"$ colcon build --symlink-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:128
msgid ""
"If you are having trouble compiling all examples and this is preventing you "
"from completing a successful build, you can use the ``--packages-skip`` "
"colcon flag to ignore the package that is causing problems. For instance, if "
"you don't want to install the large OpenCV library, you could skip building "
"the packages that depend on it using the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:131
msgid ""
"$ colcon build --symlink-install --packages-skip image_tools "
"intra_process_demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:136
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:138
msgid "Set up your environment by sourcing the following file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:140
msgid "$ . ~/ros2_rolling/install/local_setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:146
msgid ""
"Replace ``.bash`` with your shell if you're not using bash. Possible values "
"are: ``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:150
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:152
msgid ""
"In one terminal, source the setup file and then run a C++ ``talker``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:154
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:159
msgid ""
"In another terminal source the setup file and then run a Python "
"``listener``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:161
msgid ""
"$ . ~/ros2_rolling/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:166
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:171
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:173
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:176
msgid "Alternate compilers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:178
msgid ""
"Using a different compiler besides gcc to compile ROS 2 is easy. If you set "
"the environment variables ``CC`` and ``CXX`` to executables for a working C "
"and C++ compiler, respectively, and retrigger CMake configuration (by using "
"``--force-cmake-config`` or by deleting the packages you want to be "
"affected), CMake will reconfigure and use the different compiler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:182
msgid "Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:184
msgid "To configure CMake to detect and use Clang:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:186
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install clang\n"
"$ export CC=clang\n"
"$ export CXX=clang++\n"
"$ colcon build --cmake-force-configure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:194
msgid "Stay up to date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/RHEL-Development-Setup.rst:196
msgid ""
"See :doc:`Maintaining-a-Source-Checkout` to periodically refresh your source "
"installation."
msgstr ""

